dict, the first on a tie, and none when that verdict is poor","surf":"the rating of GET /v1/surf/spots/{id} (its rules are there), by its share of points: 75 % and over good, 50 % and over possible, less poor; with fewer than three criteria known, null. A primary swell worth 0 points (under 0.5 m, or 4 m and over) makes it poor whatever the other criteria give","kite":"wind within the range asked for (default 12 to 25 knots): good; within 3 knots of it: possible; else poor. Gusts above the mean wind by 5 knots or less: good; 6 to 8: possible; more: poor. Wind from the land side (offshore): possible at best","boat":"mean wind in Beaufort force (knots rounded): 4 or less good, 5 possible, 6 and over poor. Gusts: force 5 or less good, 6 to 7 possible, 8 and over poor. Sea (significant wave height): under 1.25 m good, under 2.5 m possible, else poor","shore_fishing":"only in the 2 hours before a low water, judged at the middle of the hour; outside, poor. Coefficient estimated by Vigie (not SHOM's) of the Brest high water nearest in time to that low water: 70 to 99 good, 50 to 69 possible, 100 and over possible (the SNSM says 100 and over is a danger), under 50 poor. Wind force 5 or less good, 6 possible, 7 and over poor. Sea under 1.25 m good, under 2.5 m possible, else poor. Without the low water, null","vigilance":"an official coastal warning (phenomenon coastal; in France the wave-submersion vigilance) in force at the spot: red makes every verdict poor; orange keeps the boat and the shore fishing at possible at best; yellow changes nothing. Where the warnings could not be read, nothing is capped and vigilance.status says unknown"},"derived":["spots.activities","spots.activities.verdict","spots.activities.best_slot","spots.activities.now","spots.coastal_level"],"limits":"The verdicts are rules of Vigie, written in `rules`: a few thresholds on the swell, the wind, the tide and the official coastal warnings. They do not know the beach, the bottom, the shelter of a bay or the person who goes: a beginner and an expert do not have the same limits (the wind range of the kite is the one asked for). The swell is Météo-France's MFWAM model on a grid of about 8 km; the wind is a forecast at 10 m; the tide is computed from a global model and can be an hour late or more inside a bay. Hours are whole hours.","disclaimer":"Not for safety and not for navigation: look at the sea on the spot, the flags and the lifeguards, read the tide tables and the official warnings, and follow the instructions of the authorities.","stale":false,"attribution":"Weather data by Open-Meteo.com (https://open-meteo.com/) | Generated using E.U. Copernicus Marine Service Information; https://doi.org/10.48670/moi-00017 | Surf spots: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright); chosen and their facing worked out by Vigie | Tides computed by Vigie from the EOT20 ocean tide model (Hart-Davis et al. 2021, DGFI-TUM, SEANOE, https://doi.org/10.17882/79489), CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); constants kept near the coasts and rounded by Vigie. Not for navigation"}